{"id":"09bc2b1ccf910553e6a005b3f7e46d8fdb3d0f94613f7807abf3831f0778714c","pubkey":"c7acabf1fed201a53185e4dc5e0c6bae2bc5db19d73abf840535f305d8f05180","created_at":1782517059,"content":"The 7-Eleven franchise model is a massive scam trap for immigrant families.\n\nThe Debt: A family borrows $800k+ from the bank to buy a 7-Eleven franchise.  They work 80-100 hour weeks for 20 years to pay it off.\n\nThe Trap: They don't own the building or the store. They just own a 20-year \"license\" to run it.\n\nThe Block: When the 20 years are up, they try to sell the store to a new buyer to get their $800k back. But 7-Eleven has to approve the buyer. Corporate routinely rejects buyers to run out the clock on purpose.\n\nThe Seizure: The moment the contract expires, 7-Eleven takes the store back for $0. The family is left with nothing, but still owes the 800k to the bank, while 7-Eleven sells the exact same store to a new immigrant for another $800k.\n\n7-11 is running a massive theft scam targeting immigrants and purposely stealing form them.\n\nhttps://youtube.com/watch?v=rGGQ-2Mq0eI","tags":[["alt","A short note: The 7-Eleven franchise model is a massive scam tra..."],["r","https://youtube.com/watch?v=rGGQ-2Mq0eI"],["client","Amethyst"]]}
